{"qid":"Q686","names":["Vanuatu"],"title":"Vanuatu","endonym":{"native":"Ripablik blong Vanuatu","lang":"bi"},"capsule":"Vanuatu gained independence on 30 July 1980 as the Republic of Vanuatu (Ripablik blong Vanuatu), having previously been the New Hebrides Condominium jointly administered by Britain and France since 1906. Independence followed a political crisis in which the Nagriamel movement under Jimmy Stevens, backed by French interests, attempted a secession of Espiritu Santo (the Coconut War); Papua New Guinea provided troops that suppressed the revolt in August 1980. The republic comprises some 80 islands extending roughly 1,300 km in Melanesia and is notable for its extreme linguistic diversity, with approximately 138 indigenous languages, the highest language density per capita in the world.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Vanuatu's maritime and island boundaries are internationally recognized; the land area of the archipelago is precisely mapped, though some inter-island maritime zone boundaries remain subject to regional agreement.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Vanuatu","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanuatu"},{"label":"Wikipedia: New Hebrides","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Hebrides"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Coconut War","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coconut_War"}],"britannica":"place/Vanuatu","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Vanuatu","rulers":[{"qid":"Q724686","name":"Walter Lini","start":1980,"end":1991,"image":"Walter Lini profile 1983 (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Walter%20Lini%20profile%201983%20(cropped)